      "message": "`build_image.py` supports getting the timestamp from [build.prop](https://cs.android.com/android/_/android/platform/build/+/ed045d3050d09d5eb4d186ded3e868e61f5018a6:tools/releasetools/build_image.py;l\u003d692;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0;drc\u003d56c980af5cf0d09f6cbdf500b7e32b4cba8411f1). The config object passed to `build_image.py` by both make and soong currently does not contain a `build.prop`, but it should be straightforward to do.\n\nHowever, I have some doubts over whether we should start using `BUILD_DATETIME_FILE` as the date in `build_image.py`. If devs/CI sets this value in their environment, then subsequent `adb sync` will sync the entire staging directory I think.\n\nAre there alernatives to getting flag-driven hermetic image files without breaking `adb sync` workflows?",
